{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/998442-edgar-allen","id":998442,"title":"Edgar Allen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T14:44:17-07:00","id":998442,"title":"Edgar Allen","content":"Was just listening to the Alan Parsons Project, song The Raven, and wondered - in World of Darkness terms was Edgar Allen Poe: Sluagh, Hollow One, Toreador, Fianna, Chanteur, or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T21:12:53-07:00","id":998605,"title":"","content":"He was a Mortal who saw just enough to question his sanity but not enough to lose it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T04:33:20-07:00","id":998694,"title":"","content":"He was a mortal who wrote horror stories. Didn't even need to see anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:49:30-07:00","id":998783,"title":"","content":"Edgar Allan Poe had a cameo in a Changeling game I ran once as a rather not-spooky ghost. The game made a brief detour to Richmond Virginia and the players had their characters go to the Edgar Allan Poe museum because they were looking for a vampire that had been seen the area. The Sluagh was able to see ghosts, saw Edgar Allan Poe's ghost and struck up a conversation with him - he ended up leading her to an old manuscript he had hidden under the floorboards of the building while he had been living there and she managed to get it published for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:35:09-07:00","id":999039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/998442-edgar-allen?p=998694#post998694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was a mortal who wrote horror stories. Didn't even need to see anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but Poe was too interesting a person to just leave out of the fun like that.<br /> <br /> The circumstances of his death are almost as fascinating as the stories he himself wrote.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:46:05-07:00","id":999090,"title":"","content":"Quoth the Sluagh kithbook: &quot;Poe was not a sluagh. Mind you, he should have been, but that's neither here nor there.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T01:39:11-08:00","id":999122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/998442-edgar-allen?p=999039#post999039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but Poe was too interesting a person to just leave out of the fun like that.<br /> <br /> The circumstances of his death are almost as fascinating as the stories he himself wrote.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps Poe was too interesting a person to dilute his life with contrived supernatural connections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T14:25:19-08:00","id":999432,"title":"","content":"He was a rare case of an Imbued Hunter well before the others. The stories were actually fictionalized retelling of how he eliminated several supernatural creatures (Tell Tale Heart, Pit &amp; Pendulum, Masque of Red Death, Cask of Amontillado) or investigations into the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:47:01-08:00","id":999811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or perhaps Poe was too interesting a person to dilute his life with contrived supernatural connections?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps we can just engage in the FUN of the thread's premise without feeling compelled to crap all over it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/998442-edgar-allen?p=999432#post999432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was a rare case of an Imbued Hunter well before the others. The stories were actually fictionalized retelling of how he eliminated several supernatural creatures (Tell Tale Heart, Pit &amp; Pendulum, Masque of Red Death, Cask of Amontillado) or investigations into the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually seen in the original novel of Abraham Lincoln, Vampire Hunter, where Abe and Poe nearly kill each other after mistaking each other for vamps!<br /> <br /> I'd go for Moros Mage myself, the mysterious events leading up to his death being the result of a particularly bad Paradox backlash...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:17:14-08:00","id":1011294,"title":"","content":"I figured this would spark some thought. Poe is still the master of making English sound like the most flowing language in existence. It isn't, but he sure does make it sound that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}